 HISTORY                                                            15 1451
 -------                                                            15 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory (May     15 1451
 2020) [1] using the FLASSH code [2].  The physical model is        15 1451
 based on a mixed elastic scattering treatment and includes         15 1451
 coherent elastic scattering, incoherent elastic scattering and     15 1451
 inelastic scattering components.  This evaluation is intended      15 1451
 to be used with the companion 7Li(7LiD) TSL evaluation when        15 1451
 modeling enriched 7LiD.                                            15 1451
                                                                    15 1451
 THEORY                                                             15 1451
 ------                                                             15 1451
 Lithium hydride (LiD) has a fluorite (NaCl) type face-centered     15 1451
 cubic crystal structure with four Li and D atoms per unit call.    15 1451
 The inelastic scattering cross sections were calculated in the     15 1451
 incoherent approximations using the D partial phonon density of    15 1451
 states from a VASP/PHONON calculation of 7LiD.  The LiD crystal    15 1451
 structure and lattice constant from [3] were used in the           15 1451
 VASP/PHONON calculation.  The mixed elastic scattering             15 1451
 treatment was used to account for both coherent and incoherent     15 1451
 elastic scattering effects present in this material.  The          15 1451
 coherent elastic scattering component was calculated in the        15 1451
 cubic approximation using the FLASSH generalized coherent          15 1451
 elastic scattering module using the 7LiD crystal structure and     15 1451
 measured room temperature lattice constant of 4.0684 Ang [3]       15 1451
 along with free atom coherent scattering cross sections of         15 1451
 2.483 b for D from [4] and 0.51 b for Li-7 from [5]. The           15 1451
 incoherent elastic scattering component was calculated using       15 1451
 the Debye-Waller factor derived from the D partial phonon          15 1451
 density of states and an D free atom incoherent scattering         15 1451
 cross section of 0.912004 b.  A D free atom total scattering       15 1451
 cross section of 3.395004 b was used for consistency with the      15 1451
 ENDF/B-VIII.0 D evaluation. A phonon order of 500 was used to      15 1451
 ensure both the inelastic scattering cross section and the         15 1451
 S(alpha,beta) functions at elevated temperatures were              15 1451
 adaquately converged.                                              15 1451
